    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2024-june/q6",
      "question": "<p>The motion of a particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> along the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis is modelled by the differential equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2\\frac{\\mathrm d^2x}{\\mathrm dt^2}+5\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}+2x=4t+12\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> metres from the origin <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geqslant0\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Determine the general solution of the differential equation. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li><li>Hence determine the particular solution for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}=-2\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Show that, according to the model, the minimum distance between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2+\\ln2)\"></span> metres.</li><li>Justify that this distance is a minimum.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>For large values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> the particle is expected to move with constant speed.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>Comment on the suitability of the model in light of this information. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
