      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>Determine the roots of the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^6=1\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>giving your answers in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm e^{\\mathrm i\\theta}\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Show the roots of the equation in part (a) on a single Argand diagram. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left(\\sqrt3+\\mathrm i\\right)^6=-64\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Hence, or otherwise, solve the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^6+64=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>giving your answers in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\mathrm e^{\\mathrm i\\theta}\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\"></span></p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
