      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:120mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-02-2024-june/q09-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1: central vertical cross-section ABCDEFA of a vase. A narrow neck AB of width 4 cm with vertical sides AF and BC of height 4.5 cm, then a rounded body curving out and down to a horizontal base ED, 7 cm below FC; E is below F and D is below C. Figure 2: axes x and y with origin O; the curve CD rises from D on the x-axis just right of O, bulges to the right, and ends at C above D.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows the central vertical cross-section <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCDEFA\"></span> of a vase together with measurements that have been taken from the vase.</p><p>The horizontal cross-section between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"FC\"></span> is a circle with diameter <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\,\\mathrm{cm}\"></span>.</p><p>The base of the vase <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ED\"></span> is horizontal and the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E\"></span> is vertically below <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span> and the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\"></span> is vertically below <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><p>Using these measurements, the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CD\"></span> is modelled by the parametric equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=a+3\\sin2t\\qquad y=b\\cos t\\qquad0\\leqslant t\\leqslant\\frac{\\pi}{2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> is the fixed origin, as shown in Figure 2.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> according to the model. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Using algebraic integration and showing all your working, determine, according to the model, the volume of the vase, giving your answer to the nearest <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{cm}^3\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li><li>State a limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
